        "original_id": "0c67922e-aca9-5a21-a7de-002ac581b2ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Dain Rauscher Wessels, Berenberg Bank, Royal Bank of Canada\n- People: John G. Taft, Johann Berenberg, Paul Berenberg, Berenberg family\n- Places: Minneapolis, Minnesota, Hamburg\n- Topics: brokerage, investment banking, private banking, firm origins, acquisitions\n\nFacts:\n- Berenberg Bank was founded in Hamburg in 1590 by the Belgian-origined Berenberg family.\n- Johann Berenberg became a co-owner of Berenberg Bank in 1748 together with his brother Paul Berenberg.\n- Johann Berenberg became the sole owner of Berenberg Bank after Paul Berenberg died in 1768.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels traced its origins to several smaller regional securities firms founded in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Royal Bank of Canada acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001, and John G. Taft then began working with Royal Bank of Canada.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels was a brokerage and investment banking firm based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- Berenberg Bank is a Hamburg-based multinational investment banking and private banking company.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
